<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korean bond market closed for labour day.</title>
<headline>South Korean bond market closed for labour day.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Korean bond market is closed on Thursday for labour day. The market will reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>Yields on benchmark three-year corporate bonds ended at 12.50 percent on Wednesday down from the previous close at 12.52 percent.</p>
<p>--Jane Lee (822) 727 5648</p>
